-- title:
--   Maximal Hecke ideal attached to a residual eigenvector on J₀(M')[p]
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ prime and $p\neq 2$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $p\nmid M'$, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers. Let $\bar\theta$ assign an element of $k$ to each generator in [`CohCarrier.Gen M' S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13), namely the symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$, the symbols $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M'$, and the diamonds indexed by $(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is, a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite subextension; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} k$ has no Galois-stable submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Assume further the trace condition: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$. Equip $J_0(M')$, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$M'$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the module structure over $\mathbb{T}=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ given by `heckeModuleBar`, write $J_p$ for the submodule annihilated by the ideal generated by the constant $p$, and for $t\in\mathbb{T}$ let $\mathrm{op}(t)$ be the $k$-linear base change to $k\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}J_p$ of multiplication by $t$. Then, assuming there exists $w\neq 0$ in $k\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}J_p$ with $\mathrm{op}(X_\ell)w=\bar\theta(T_\ell)w$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M'$, with $\mathrm{op}(X_q)w=\bar\theta(U_q)w$ for all primes $q\mid M'$, and with $w=\bar\theta(\mathrm{dia}\,d)\,w$ for all $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$, the conclusion is that there are a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $\mathbb{T}$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m}\to k$ such that $p\in\mathfrak{m}$, $\iota(X_\ell \bmod \mathfrak m)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$, $\iota(X_q\bmod\mathfrak m)=\bar\theta(U_q)$ for primes $q\mid M'$, and $\mathrm{op}(t)w=\iota(t\bmod\mathfrak{m})\,w$ for every $t\in\mathbb{T}$ and every $w\in k\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}J_p$ satisfying the same three eigenvector conditions. No uniqueness of $\mathfrak m$ or of $\iota$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the passage from an eigensystem pinned on the Hecke generators away from $S$ to a maximal ideal of the full Hecke algebra, in the form used for the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian $J_0(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: once $\mathfrak m$ and $\iota$ are produced, every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts on any such eigenvector through the residue field of $\mathfrak m$. It is used in the construction of the Hecke-stable pairing between $H^1$ and the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of $J_0(M')$, in [`CohCarrier.exists_ideal_H1_top_to_dual_baseChange_heckeTorsion_jZero_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_ideal_H1_top_to_dual_baseChange_heckeTorsion_jZero_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible).
